WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.536 --> 00:00:13.656
In wedding photos and videos, lighting reflection tends to make faces look about 130% larger than they really are.

2
00:00:13.992 --> 00:00:24.600
To counter this, MakeupForL goes beyond ordinary makeup, focusing on "contour makeup" that precisely shapes the face's proportions and dimension.

3
00:00:24.936 --> 00:00:33.480
Using three or more foundation shades, we apply darker shading along the face line to shrink the outer area,

4
00:00:33.816 --> 00:00:43.608
then highlight the T-zone to draw the features toward the center — making the face look visibly smaller.

5
00:00:43.944 --> 00:00:49.272
Hairstyling is another key factor in how large the face appears.

6
00:00:49.608 --> 00:00:58.632
For a round face, adding volume at the crown draws the eye up and down, extending vertical length,

7
00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:08.304
while keeping the sides close to the face with minimal volume makes it look slimmer and smaller.

8
00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:20.904
Also, straight brows on a round face can widen it visually, so a slightly arched brow shape works better to define the face.

9
00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:34.248
Finally, a bright smile stretches the muscles around the mouth up and down, slimming the face — making a genuine smile the best "face-lift" makeup can't match.

10
00:01:34.584 --> 00:01:46.776
This kind of personalized design works best when finalized in a one-on-one consultation, trying it out in front of the mirror together with your artist.
